  "question": "A very small hole in an electric furnace is used for heating metals. The hole nearly acts as a black body. The area of the hole is $200\\ \\text{mm}^2$. To keep a metal at $727°$C, the heat energy flowing through this hole per second, in joules, is ($\\sigma = 5.67 \\times 10^{-8}\\ \\text{W m}^{-2}\\text{K}^{-4}$)",
